<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pintia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pintia is an archaeological site of the Vaccaei near Padilla de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douro">Duero</a> in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valladolid">Valladolid</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, occupied from about the 4th century BCE into Roman times. It comprises a fortified town, a craftsmen's quarter and the necropolis of Las Ruedas, where grave goods, weapons and stone markers reveal a society led by a warrior elite. It is one of the best-studied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> sites of the Douro valley.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pintia.jpg" alt="Pintia" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miguel Alan Córdova Silva · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Necr%C3%B3polis_de_Las_Ruedas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
